From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Restore VK_EXT_opacity_micromap as a fallback backend.

Opacity micromaps are gated on VK_KHR_opacity_micromap, which is very new;
drivers that only expose the older VK_EXT_opacity_micromap report no OMM
support at all. Upstream removed the EXT backend deliberately (3c3b1deb and
following) to simplify the code, accepting that EXT-only devices lose the
feature. This restores it as a fallback.

KHR remains the first choice. EXT is selected only when the device does not
expose KHR, via using_khr_opacity_micromap; on a KHR-capable device every new
block is dead and the existing code path is unchanged. That property was
audited three times over the course of development.

The two extensions do not share an object model: KHR builds a micromap as an
acceleration structure with type OPACITY_MICROMAP_KHR, while EXT has a
separate VkMicromapEXT with its own create/build/size entry points. The EXT
side therefore needs its own object lifetime, va_map tracking and build
dispatch rather than a constant swap.

Per-geometry usage counts on BLAS linkage are left at zero by default, which
is what the original EXT backend did for the three years it was the only
backend. A real histogram, recorded when the OMM array is built, can be
enabled with VKD3D_CONFIG=omm_ext_linkage_usage_counts.

NOTE: this has been reviewed but never built or exercised on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/include/private/config_flag_decl.h b/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
--- a/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
+++ b/include/private/config_flag_decl.h
@@ -72,3 +72,10 @@ VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("disallow_committed_texture_suballocation", DISALLOW_COMMITTED
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("allow_image_heap_suballocation", ALLOW_IMAGE_HEAP_SUBALLOCATION)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("debug_wave64_simulation", DEBUG_WAVE64_SIMULATION)
 VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("fail_unsupported_state_template", FAIL_UNSUPPORTED_STATE_TEMPLATE)
+/* Opt-in: republish the remembered OMM usage histogram on VK_EXT_opacity_micromap BLAS linkage.
+ * Off by default, i.e. usageCountsCount = 0, which is what the upstream EXT backend shipped before
+ * it was removed. It has to stay off by default because D3D12 never hands us a histogram on the
+ * linkage itself: a prebuild sizing query issued before the OMM array build is recorded observes 0
+ * while the later build would observe N, and the two must agree. Experimental, for A/B testing
+ * against a real EXT-only driver. No effect on the KHR backend. */
+VKD3D_DECL_CONFIG("omm_ext_linkage_usage_counts", OMM_EXT_LINKAGE_USAGE_COUNTS)
diff --git a/include/private/config_flags.h b/include/private/config_flags.h
--- a/include/private/config_flags.h
+++ b/include/private/config_flags.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ struct vkd3d_config_flags_bitfield
 	 * we may end up with stray uninitialized bits which can subtly break bitwise operations later.
 	 * Adding more configs will cause the static assert below to fail,
 	 * which indicates the need to subtract a reserved bit. */
-	uint32_t reserved0 : 23;
+	uint32_t reserved0 : 22;
 };
 
 STATIC_ASSERT(sizeof(struct vkd3d_config_flags_bitfield) == 12);
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/acceleration_structure.c b/libs/vkd3d/acceleration_structure.c
--- a/libs/vkd3d/acceleration_structure.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/acceleration_structure.c
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ bool vkd3d_acceleration_structure_convert_inputs(struct d3d12_device *device,
         const D3D12_BUILD_RAYTRACING_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_INPUTS *desc,
         VkAccelerationStructureBuildGeometryInfoKHR *build_info,
